## Code Changes Required Before Deployment

These are the **source-code changes** needed so the app works correctly when deployed. No changes break local dev.

---

### Backend — `server/`

#### [MODIFY] [server.js](file:///c:/Users/yvasa/Videos/Projects/rental-management/server/server.js)

Two issues to fix:
1. **PORT fallback** — Render dynamically assigns a port; add a fallback so `process.env.PORT` is never `undefined`.
2. **CORS** — Lock down `cors()` to only accept requests from your Vercel frontend URL (you'll add this after deploy).

```js
// Current
app.use(cors());
app.listen(process.env.PORT, () => { ... });

// After
app.use(cors({
  origin: process.env.CLIENT_URL || '*',
  credentials: true,
}));
app.listen(process.env.PORT || 5000, () => { ... });
```

#### [MODIFY] [config/db.js](file:///c:/Users/yvasa/Videos/Projects/rental-management/server/config/db.js)

Aiven and Railway MySQL **require SSL**. Switch from `createConnection` to a **connection pool** (more resilient for cloud), and add SSL support.

```js
// After
const mysql = require('mysql2');
require('dotenv').config();

const db = mysql.createPool({
  host:     process.env.DB_HOST,
  port:     process.env.DB_PORT || 3306,
  user:     process.env.DB_USER,
  password: process.env.DB_PASSWORD,
  database: process.env.DB_NAME,
  ssl: process.env.DB_SSL === 'true' ? { rejectUnauthorized: false } : false,
  waitForConnections: true,
  connectionLimit: 10,
});

module.exports = db.promise();
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Switching to `pool.promise()` means all controllers that currently do `db.query(...)` with a callback will need to be updated to use `async/await` or `.then()`. Check every file in `server/controllers/`.

