## Deployment Steps

### Step 1 — Set Up MySQL Database

**Option A — Aiven MySQL (recommended, free tier)**
1. Sign up at [aiven.io](https://aiven.io) → Create service → MySQL → Free plan.
2. Once running, go to **Connection Information** → copy:
   - Host, Port, User, Password, Database name
3. Download the **CA Certificate** if required (some drivers need it).
4. Enable `DB_SSL=true` in your Render env vars.

**Option B — Railway MySQL**
1. Sign up at [railway.app](https://railway.app) → New Project → Add MySQL.
2. Go to **Variables** tab → copy `MYSQL_HOST`, `MYSQL_PORT`, `MYSQL_USER`, `MYSQL_PASSWORD`, `MYSQL_DATABASE`.
3. SSL is optional on Railway (set `DB_SSL=false` if connection fails with SSL).

---

### Step 2 — Deploy Backend to Render

1. Push your latest code to GitHub.
2. Go to [render.com](https://render.com) → New → **Web Service**.
3. Connect your GitHub repo → select the `rental-management` root.
4. Configure:
   | Setting | Value |
   |---|---|
   | **Root Directory** | `server` |
   | **Runtime** | Node |
   | **Build Command** | `npm install` |
   | **Start Command** | `npm start` |
   | **Instance Type** | Free |
5. Under **Environment Variables**, add all vars from `.env.example` using real values from your DB provider.
6. Click **Deploy**. Note the URL: `https://your-app.onrender.com`.

> [!WARNING]
> Free-tier Render services **spin down after 15 minutes of inactivity**. First request after sleep takes ~30s. Upgrade to Starter ($7/mo) to avoid this.

---

### Step 3 — Deploy Frontend to Vercel

1. Go to [vercel.com](https://vercel.com) → New Project → Import your GitHub repo.
2. Configure:
   | Setting | Value |
   |---|---|
   | **Root Directory** | `client` |
   | **Framework Preset** | Vite |
   | **Build Command** | `npm run build` |
   | **Output Directory** | `dist` |
3. Under **Environment Variables**, add:
   ```
   VITE_API_URL = https://your-app.onrender.com
   ```
4. Deploy. Note your Vercel URL: `https://rent-flow.vercel.app`.

---

### Step 4 — Update CORS on Backend

After you have the Vercel URL, go to Render → your service → **Environment** → update:
```
CLIENT_URL = https://rent-flow.vercel.app
```
Trigger a redeploy.

